# Branch consistency (before commit)

On a feature branch, run the full checklist in **`.cursorrules`** → **Before committing** (expanded). Summary:

1. `git diff origin/main HEAD --stat` — skim all behavior changes.
2. **Code ↔ docs** — new/changed `src/emet/simulation/`, `src/emet/app/`, or CLI subcommands → `docs/cli.md`, topic doc, or `docs/simulation_modules.md`.
3. **CLI ↔ docs** — `emet <cmd> --help` matches documented defaults (`resolve_serve_robot()`, dataclass defaults).
4. **Env vars** — new `EMET_*` in changed Python → `docs/environment_variables.md` or topic env doc.
5. **Defaults** — core `emet` CLI, `packages/emet_molmospaces/emet_molmospaces/runner.py`, and `.cursorrules` agree (MolmoSpaces default robot: **stretch**).
6. **Tests** — update CLI help tests when adding subcommands.
7. **Agent modes** — if touching `emet.agent.skills`, chat `get_tools`, or `build_agentic_eqa_tools`: keep CHAT vs EQA_EPISODE packs disjoint; run `uv run emet test src/test/agent/test_skill_packs.py`; sync [`docs/AGENT_RUN.md`](../../docs/AGENT_RUN.md) and [`.cursor/rules/agent-modes.mdc`](agent-modes.mdc). Do not rename EQA tools without updating traces/docs.
8. **Eval / GPU changes** — if touching Habitat runners, overnight scripts, eval harnesses, or `emet eval` / `gpu_preflight`: keep [`docs/cli.md`](../../docs/cli.md) (`emet eval` section), [`src/emet/utils/gpu_preflight.py`](../../src/emet/utils/gpu_preflight.py), and overnight scripts aligned; document **`emet eval`** as primary (bash `gpu_preflight.sh` as delegate). Confirm [`docs/experiments/cross_track_smoke.md`](../../docs/experiments/cross_track_smoke.md); run tier 0 + at least one track smoke before claiming merge-ready.
9. Trim AI slop; prefer clear failures over silent fallbacks.
10. **Copyright:** any *new* file in the commit must be Chris Paxton (not Hello Robot) — see [copyright.mdc](copyright.mdc).
